  "identifier": "uni",
  "name": "UNI",
  "description": "The largest pretrained vision foundation model for computational pathology — a ViT-L/16 encoder trained with DINOv2 self-supervised learning on 100M+ H&E image patches from 100,000+ whole-slide images (Mass-100K dataset, MGH/BWH private collections + GTEx). Achieves state-of-the-art performance across 34 clinical pathology tasks including cancer subtyping, survival prediction, and mutation detection. Does not use TCGA/CAMELYON/CPTAC for pretraining, eliminating benchmark contamination risk. Published in Nature Medicine 2024. 0.3B parameters (ViT-Large). CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0, 45k+ monthly HuggingFace downloads.",
  "url": "https://huggingface.co/MahmoodLab/UNI",
